\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Attention forward pass latency on TPU v6e-1 (log-log scale). Softmax-based methods (Normal, Flash) are faster per-operation but cannot learn alignment ($\sim $20\% accuracy). Pallas Sinkhorn is slower due to 15 iterative normalization passes but achieves 72\% accuracy. Banded Sinkhorn provides a $\sim $$2\times $ speedup over full Sinkhorn while extending to 131K.}}{9}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:latency}{{5}{9}{Attention forward pass latency on TPU v6e-1 (log-log scale). Softmax-based methods (Normal, Flash) are faster per-operation but cannot learn alignment ($\sim $20\% accuracy). Pallas Sinkhorn is slower due to 15 iterative normalization passes but achieves 72\% accuracy. Banded Sinkhorn provides a $\sim $$2\times $ speedup over full Sinkhorn while extending to 131K}{figure.5}{}}
